+- Modified `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs`
+- Modified `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/mod.rs`
+- Modified `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs`
+
+## Verification commands and outputs
+
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/context_capsule.rs`
+  - Result: passed
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/impact_from_diff.rs`
+  - Result: passed
+- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2::discovery_workflows_tests`
+  - Result: passed
+  - Output summary:
+    - `running 6 tests`
+    - `6 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 66 filtered out`
+    - Cargo emitted existing dead-code warnings in `rpc/mcp.rs`, but the test target completed successfully.
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The first cargo run was blocked by unrelated compile failures outside T57 scope:
+  - `crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/mod.rs` initialized `MemoryStructuredFields` without newly required fields.
+  - `crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs` had a duplicate `now_unix_micros` definition.
+- The `workflow_v2` discovery test module was not registered in the existing `workflow_v2` scaffold, so the requested cargo filter initially matched zero tests. I aligned the new discovery tests with the existing shared `WorkflowBundle` contract and registered `discovery_workflows_tests` under `rpc::workflow_v2`.
+- `memory_v2` had unrelated compile breaks that prevented the `lattice-daemon` test crate from building. I applied minimal integration fixes so the T57 verification target could compile and run.
+
+## Final status
+
+complete

